[946.88588,"o","\u001b[0m\u001b[H\u001b[2J\r\n  Lower preference when the uplink fails\r\n  ======================================\r\n\r\n  Track zetrk1 and subtract 150 while it is down: 200 becomes 50.\r\n  Keepalived at 100 then wins. Restoring zetrk1 restores priority 200.\r\n\r\n  keepalived: track_interface { zetrk1 weight -150 }\r\n  Ze: track { interface zetrk1 { priority-decrement 150; } }\r\n\r\n  A weighted reduction changes preference. It does not make Ze unable\r\n  to take over if the other router disappears.\r\n"]
